# COLUMN DEFINITIONS:
# category_code      : Category code (greenmetric, qs, the, webometrics)
# year              : Year of ranking (e.g., 2024, 2025)
# period            : Period (Annual, January, July, etc.) - can be empty
# world_rank        : World ranking as displayed (can be text like "1401+", "TBD")
# world_rank_numeric: Numeric value for sorting (integer only, leave empty if not applicable)
# national_rank     : National ranking (Indonesia) - integer or empty
# regional_rank     : Regional ranking (Asia/ASEAN) - integer or empty
# overall_score     : Overall score (decimal) - can be empty
# rank_change       : Change from previous period (integer: -10 = improved 10 positions, +5 = dropped 5)
# trend             : Trend indicator (up, down, stable, new)
# source_url        : Source URL for verification
# notes             : Additional notes or description

# TIPS:
# 1. Keep the header row as-is
# 2. category_code must match existing categories
# 3. Combination of category_code + year + period must be unique
# 4. If a record exists, it will be UPDATED. If not, it will be INSERTED
# 5. Empty cells are treated as NULL
# 6. Use quotes if your text contains commas (CSV standard)
# 7. world_rank can be text (e.g., "1401+", "TBD"), but world_rank_numeric must be integer
